<item>
            <title>[LU-20529] garbage collector:  changelog user deregistered because the unprocessed changelog value is invalid </title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20529</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Lustre version : lfs 2.14.0_ddn246&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Based on the log, the problem is linked to the current index value and the user index value not updating correctly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#de350b&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Jun 17 20:45:54 prj-mds01 kernel: Lustre: 2862542:0:(mdd_trans.c:180:mdd_chlg_garbage_collect()) tier2-MDD0000: force deregister of changelog user cl2 idle for 1158s with 2098261127 unprocessed records&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The number of unprocessed events is equal to 2.098 billion during a changelog idle timeout equal to 19min (that is very small !!!! ).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cl2 was stopped for only ~20 minutes (&lt;tt&gt;1158s&lt;/tt&gt; in the log), the implied generation rate would be:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2098261127/1158 &#8776; &lt;b&gt;1.8 million changelog records per second&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But based on the measurement done by the customer, the rate between two current index with timeout equal to 60s is only 64 changelog records per second.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mon Jul 13 15:00:20 CEST 2026 =&amp;gt; lag=121971118 idle=1609s user_index=6412160230 current_index=6534131348&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mon Jul 13 15:01:20 CEST 2026 =&amp;gt; lag=121974919 idle=1669s user_index=6412160230 current_index=6534135149&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(6534135149 - 6534131348)/ 60 = 3801/60 &#8776; 64 &lt;b&gt;changelog records per second&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;This the reason why we suspect a bug in the computation of the unprocessed changelogs during the start of garbage collector.&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
